 succeeded in 213ms:
21:        ONE dispatch, so the host was unresponsive for the duration and
22:        n_translated_instrs (an int, reset per run_instr, and this walk is
23:        REPLAYABLE) was drivable into signed overflow with ~18-24 MB of
24:        non-NUL memory at the default -M 64.
25:
26:HOW THE YIELD IS WITNESSED WITHOUT A CLOCK.  `testarm` carries the `mp` test
27:device; its NCYCLES register at 0x110000d0 returns cpu->ninstrs, and ninstrs is
28:committed only when run_instr RETURNS. So a guest that samples it either side of
29:a long walk reads ~0 if the whole walk stayed inside one dispatch, and a real
30:count if the fold yielded and the dispatcher went round again. Wall-clock timing
31:would not be acceptable in a gate; this is deterministic.
32:
33:BANDS, NOT COUNTS -- and the real reason is staleness, not the constants.  The
34:numbers do depend on N_SAFE_DYNTRANS_LIMIT (8191) and the 120-dispatch group,
35:but the dominant imprecision is that ninstrs is committed only when run_instr
36:RETURNS, so the guest's second sample is stale by up to one batch. Measured on a
37:1 MB walk: folded 3,144,852 against an architectural 3n = 3,145,728 (0.99972),
38:-J genuine 3,138,120 (0.99758) -- deficits of 876 and 7608, both inside one
39:batch (69 x 120 = 8280). The mp register's own comment calls its value
40:"approximately the number of cycles" for the same reason.
41:
42:CONSEQUENCE, stated so nobody over-reads these rows: this probe CANNOT verify
43:the 3n-1 billing constant to better than about 8K instructions. What these rows
44:prove is that the walk yields at all (0 vs not-0) and that the total is the
45:right order of magnitude. The exactness of 3n-1 rests on the source derivation
46:plus that 1 MB differential above, not on any row here.
47:"""
48:import os
49:import pty
50:import re
51:import select
52:import sys
53:import time
54:
55:BIN = sys.argv[1]
56:
57:CODE = 0x8000
58:DEST = 0x9000
59:STRBASE = 0x10000
60:STRLEN = 0x4000                 # 16 KB of non-NUL; NUL at STRBASE+STRLEN
61:ALIAS_STR = 0x9100              # short string for the #355 row
62:
63:#  --- the #356 walk: base r4, dest r3 (distinct -- post-#355 the aliased form
64:#  --- is refused, so the yield row must use a genuine strlen shape).
65:PROG_WALK = [
66:    0xE3A07C90,   # 0  mov r7,#0x9000       publish base
67:    0xE3A08411,   # 1  mov r8,#0x11000000   mp device
68:    0xE28880D0,   # 2  add r8,r8,#0xd0      -> NCYCLES
69:    0xE5986000,   # 3  ldr r6,[r8]          D = ninstrs before
70:    0xE3A04801,   # 4  mov r4,#0x10000
71:    0xE2444001,   # 5  sub r4,r4,#1         first pre-indexed load hits 0x10000
72:    0xE5F43001,   # 6  S: ldrb r3,[r4,#1]!
73:    0xE3530000,   # 7  cmps r3,#0
74:    0x1AFFFFFC,   # 8  bne S                arms COMBINE(strlen)
75:    0xE5989000,   # 9  ldr r9,[r8]          E = ninstrs after
76:    0xE5876000,   # 10 str r6,[r7]
77:    0xE5879004,   # 11 str r9,[r7,#4]
78:    0xE5874008,   # 12 str r4,[r7,#8]       end address -- must be 0x14000
79:    0xEAFFFFFE,   # 13 b .
80:]
81:
82:#  --- the #355 row: base == dest == r3. Publishes a sentinel ONLY if the loop
83:#  --- was exited, plus r3 itself so a program that never ran cannot pass by
84:#  --- looking like "still looping" (the forward-progress assertion).
85:PROG_ALIAS = [
86:    0xE3A07C90,   # 0 mov r7,#0x9000
87:    0xE3A03C91,   # 1 mov r3,#0x9100        base == dest
88:    0xE3A05055,   # 2 mov r5,#0x55          sentinel
89:    0xE5F33001,   # 3 S: ldrb r3,[r3,#1]!
90:    0xE3530000,   # 4 cmps r3,#0
91:    0x1AFFFFFC,   # 5 bne S
92:    0xE5875000,   # 6 str r5,[r7]           reached only if the loop EXITED
93:    0xE5873004,   # 7 str r3,[r7,#4]        r3 for the progress assertion
94:    0xEAFFFFFE,   # 8 b .
95:]
96:
97:
98:def session(prog, extra, nwords, grace, load_str, read_r3=False):
99:    """Run one read-ahead-ON session. Returns the published words, plus r3 read
100:    from the DEBUGGER when read_r3 is set.
101:
102:    r3 must come from `reg`, not from a guest store: on the #355 row the loop
103:    never exits post-fix, so any store placed after the loop is unreachable and
104:    an assertion made through it could never pass. (That was the first version
105:    of the progress row here, and it failed for exactly that reason -- a row
106:    that cannot pass is the mirror of a row that cannot fail, and this harness
107:    retires both.)"""
108:    stub = "/tmp/gx_strlen_stub.bin"
109:    with open(stub, "wb") as f:
110:        f.write((0xe1a00000).to_bytes(4, "little"))
111:    args = [BIN, "-V", "-A"] + extra + ["-E", "testarm", "-M", "64",
112:                                        "0x%x:%s" % (CODE, stub)]
113:    if load_str:
114:        s = "/tmp/gx_strlen_str.bin"
115:        with open(s, "wb") as f:
116:            f.write(b"\xff" * STRLEN + b"\x00" * 4)
493:#
494:# The yield is witnessed WITHOUT a clock: the test machine's mp device exposes
495:# cpu->ninstrs at 0x110000d0, and ninstrs is committed only when run_instr
496:# returns, so a guest sampling it either side of a 16 KB walk reads ~0 if the
497:# walk never left one dispatch. All numeric rows assert BANDS, because the exact
498:# counts depend on N_SAFE_DYNTRANS_LIMIT (8191) and the 120-dispatch group
499:# boundary -- named so a change to either moves the bands deliberately.
500:#
501:# Swept against a binary built from the pre-fix HEAD: 3 of 7, failing exactly
502:# the four discriminators -- `yields` and `bill band` both read 0 (the walk
503:# never left the dispatch), `alias exits` read 0x55 (the fold took the wrong
504:# exit) and `alias moved` read "no" (it had exited after three bytes). The
505:# three PINs pass on both builds. On the fixed build: 7/7.
506:STRLOG=$LOGDIR/gate_arm_strlen.log
507:python3 arm_strlen_probe.py "$PMAX" > "$STRLOG" 2>&1 || true
508:
509:if ! grep -q "STRLEN_RESULT=" "$STRLOG"; then
510:    note "strlen probe produced no result line; last lines follow"
511:    tail -5 "$STRLOG" | sed 's/^/       /'
512:    gate_skip "strlen probe did not complete"
513:fi
514:
515:grep -E " ok$| FAIL$" "$STRLOG" | sed 's/^/       /'
516:
517:sctrl=$(grep -o "STRLEN_CONTROL=[A-Z]*" "$STRLOG" | tail -1 | cut -d= -f2)
518:check "strlen control: -J reference walked and yielded" "${sctrl:-missing}" "OK"
519:
520:sres=$(grep -o "STRLEN_RESULT=[0-9]*/[0-9]*" "$STRLOG" | tail -1 | cut -d= -f2)
521:sgot=${sres%/*}; swant=${sres#*/}
522:check "strlen rows run"     "$swant" 7
523:check "strlen rows correct" "$sgot"  "$swant"
524:
525:for v in "A strlen -J ref" "A strlen -J end addr" "A strlen yields" \
526:         "A strlen bill band" "A strlen end addr" "A strlen alias exits" \
527:         "A strlen alias moved"; do
528:    n=$(count "$STRLOG" "^$v  .*ok$")
529:    check "  strlen row: $v" "$n" 1
530:done
