The DATA guard is unreachable through the proposed PORT logic: initialization and every permitted store leave the selector in 0–7. I also found a factual error in the control description: plain RAM would return the last DATA write, `2`, not the earlier `123`. The expected device result, `0`, still distinguishes it from RAM.
